      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const alaRecord = $('Step 9a - Fetch ALA Record').first().json;\nconst rawText = alaRecord['Raw Tex'] || alaRecord['Raw Text'] || 'Not available';\n\nconst recentRecords = $('Step 9a-2 - Fetch Recent RDA Drafts').first().json;\nconst recentList = recentRecords.list || [];\nconst recentOpenings = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < recentList.length; i++) {\n  const draft = recentList[i]['Public Response Draft'];\n  if (draft && draft.length > 10) {\n    const firstSentence = draft.split(/[.!—]/)[0].trim();\n    if (firstSentence.length > 5) recentOpenings.push(firstSentence);\n  }\n}\n\nconst inp = $('Step 8 - Build Final Output').first().json;\n\nif (!inp.public_response_draft || inp.public_response_draft.length < 20)\n  throw new Error('public_response_draft missing or too short from Step 8. ala_record_id: ' + inp.ala_record_id);\nif (!inp.internal_followup_draft || inp.internal_followup_draft.length < 10)\n  throw new Error('internal_followup_draft missing or too short from Step 8. ala_record_id: ' + inp.ala_record_id);\n\nconst audit_system_prompt =\n'Your role: evaluate and correct a draft that must read as written by a person. When correcting failures, preserve the human quality of the original. Never introduce language that sounds machine-generated.\\n\\n' +\n'You are an editorial auditor for SubtextCX.\\n\\n' +\n'You receive: the original guest review and a proposed public response draft.\\n\\n' +\n'Your job: evaluate the draft against each checklist item. If ALL items pass, return the draft unchanged. If ANY item fails, rewrite ONLY the failing element. Never rewrite passing elements. Never introduce details not present in the original review.\\n\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n' +\n'COMPLIANCE CHECKLIST\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n\\n' +\n'1. NAMED STAFF\\n' +\n'If the review names a specific staff member (server, host, bartender, chef), that exact name MUST appear in the draft.\\n' +\n'FAIL: Staff name present in review but absent or replaced with \"your server\", \"our team\", or any generic substitute.\\n\\n' +\n'2. REVIEW DEPTH MATCH\\n' +\n'A review longer than 80 words must reference at least 2 specific elements the guest named --- dish, person, occasion, or moment. A short review must not receive a padded response.\\n' +\n'FAIL: Long detailed review receives a response with zero specific references to what the guest named.\\n\\n' +\n'3. CLOSING SPECIFICITY\\n' +\n'The closing must derive from something specific in this guest\\'s review --- the occasion, the dish, the guest\\'s own words, or their visit frequency.\\n' +\n'FAIL conditions:\\n' +\n'- Closing is a generic formula such as \"We\\'d love to welcome you back\" or \"we hope to see you soon\"\\n' +\n'- Closing repeats any specific noun already used earlier in the same draft --- including dish names, item names, or person names\\n' +\n'- Closing contains vague language such as \"across both\", \"all of it\", \"that same experience\", \"that kind of evening\" with no specific referent\\n' +\n'If the review is very short, close with a brief sincere acknowledgment --- not a formula.\\n\\n' +\n'4. LOYALTY SIGNAL\\n' +\n'If the guest signals they are a regular or frequent visitor (words: always, every time, weekly, come back regularly, each visit, been here before), the response must acknowledge the ongoing relationship --- not treat them as a first-time visitor.\\n' +\n'FAIL: Regular guest receives a first-time-visitor closing or no acknowledgment of the pattern.\\n\\n' +\n'5. CONSTRUCTIVE SUGGESTION\\n' +\n'If the guest makes a specific positive suggestion, acknowledge it by name.\\n' +\n'FAIL: Specific suggestion deflected with generic language or ignored entirely.\\n\\n' +\n'6. PROHIBITED CONTENT\\n' +\n'The draft must contain no email address, URL, any reference to contact methods or channels (including \"our profile\", \"our website\", \"our direct messaging\", \"contact details\"), placeholder text such as [contact] or [name], or the phrase \"We apologize for any inconvenience.\"\\n' +\n'FAIL: Any of the above present anywhere in the draft.\\n\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n' +\n'FORMULA CHECKLIST\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n\\n' +\n'7. OVERUSED VERBS\\n' +\n'FAIL: The draft uses \"landed\" more than once, or uses \"landed\" as the primary verb of acknowledgment when a more specific verb fits better.\\n' +\n'FIX: Replace with: resonated, came through, delivered, felt right, worked, made an impression, held up, came together.\\n\\n' +\n'8. OVERUSED PHRASES\\n' +\n'FAIL: The draft contains any of the following:\\n' +\n'- \"means a great deal to our team\" --- replace with a specific acknowledgment tied to the guest\\'s signal\\n' +\n'- \"our team works hard to\" --- replace with what the team specifically does in this context\\n' +\n'- \"all of it\" --- replace with the actual elements the guest named\\n' +\n'- \"that kind of evening\" --- replace with the specific occasion or experience the guest described\\n' +\n'- \"exactly what we work toward\" --- replace with what specifically was achieved in this visit\\n' +\n'- \"Knowing\" as an opening word --- replace with a structurally different construction\\n\\n' +\n'9. BRAND PHRASE COUNT\\n' +\n'FAIL: More than one of these phrases appears in the same draft:\\n' +\n'- \"Thank you for dining with us\"\\n' +\n'- \"We\\'d love to welcome you back\"\\n' +\n'- \"We take great pride in every guest experience\"\\n' +\n'FIX: Remove all but the most contextually natural one. If none fits naturally, remove all.\\n\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n' +\n'OPENING VARIATION\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n\\n' +\n'10. OPENING REPETITION\\n' +\n'FAIL: The opening sentence of this draft uses the same grammatical structure or lead word as any of the recent openings listed below. If no recent openings are listed, this item passes automatically.\\n' +\n'FIX: Rewrite the opening sentence only using a structurally different construction.\\n\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n' +\n'GUEST NAME\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n\\n' +\n'11. GUEST NAME PRESENT\\n' +\n'If the GUEST NAME provided is not \"Not available\", that name MUST appear in the draft.\\n' +\n'FAIL: Guest name is available but absent from the draft entirely.\\n' +\n'FIX: For T1 records, insert \"[Name],\" at the start of the opening sentence. For T2 and T3 records, insert \"Hello [Name] ---\" before the existing opening content. Do not rewrite anything else.';\n\nconst recentOpeningsBlock = recentOpenings.length > 0\n  ? '\\n\\nRECENT OPENINGS USED — do not repeat these structures:\\n' +\n    recentOpenings.map((o, i) => (i + 1) + '. \"' + o + '\"').join('\\n')\n  : '';\n\nconst closingBlock =\n'\\n\\n────────────────────────────────────\\n' +\n'CORRECTION RULES\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n' +\n'- Correct ONLY the specific element that failed. Do not rewrite the whole draft.\\n' +\n'- Never introduce content, details, or references not present in the original guest review.\\n' +\n'- Maintain the same tone_style, formality_level, and brand voice throughout.\\n' +\n'- After correction the draft must still pass all other checklist items.\\n\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n' +\n'CRITICAL JSON RULES\\n' +\n'────────────────────────────────────\\n' +\n'- Return valid JSON only. No preamble. No explanation. No markdown fences.\\n' +\n'- failed_items must contain checklist item NAMES as strings --- never numbers.\\n' +\n'  Correct: [\"CLOSING SPECIFICITY\", \"OPENING REPETITION\"]\\n' +\n'  Wrong: [3, 10]\\n' +\n'- All string values must use straight double quotes only.\\n' +\n'- Do not truncate the draft field. It must be complete.\\n\\n' +\n'RETURN this exact structure:\\n' +\n'{\\n' +\n'  \"audit_passed\": true,\\n' +\n'  \"failed_items\": [],\\n' +\n'  \"final_public_response_draft\": \"complete corrected or unchanged public